# Amazon Clone 🛒

A simple Amazon homepage clone built using HTML and CSS to practice frontend web development. This project recreates the basic layout and visual design of Amazon's homepage.

## 🚀 Features

- Navigation bar with Amazon-style branding
- Search bar UI
- Delivery location section
- Navigation menu and product categories
- Product category cards
- Footer section inspired by Amazon's website

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- **HTML5** — Structure of the webpage
- **CSS3** — Styling, layout, spacing, and design

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
amazon-clone/
├── index.html
├── style.css
└── amazon_logo.png
```

*Note: Update the file structure above if your project contains additional files or folders.*

## 💻 How to Run Locally

1. Clone this repository:

   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/amazon-clone.git
   ```

2. Navigate to the project directory:

   ```bash
   cd amazon-clone
   ```

3. Open `index.html` in your browser.

## 📚 What I Learned

- Structuring webpages using HTML
- Styling elements using CSS
- Working with margins, padding, and dimensions
- Using background images and positioning
- Creating navigation bars and layouts

## 🔮 Future Improvements

